Z||000011||Ronen||05-04-2001||12:44 PM||||I work for a tow company as the accountant. We found an abandoned 85 Fiero GT on the side of the road and as soon as it was up for sale I bought it. I am super happy to join this family of Fiero owners. What was wrong with this abandoned was the ignition module was damaged. Once it was repaired it worked fine, but for the major oil leak. I am being told it is coming from the oil pressure sending unit. When you turn on the car the oil gage goes all the way to the above the number 80 and beyond. I looked for the oil sending unit next to the oil filter but it is not there. There is a puddle of fresh oil on the engine block right under the distributor cap area about 3 inches under the area. Is this where the sending unit actually is? How much is it to repair?||||reg||5
Z||000012||Au nrod||05-04-2001||05:01 PM||||sorry man, i'm not a very good mechanic. tell you what though. post this question as a new topic and i'm sure some of the other forum people will know just what your problem is and where it is located. mean time, keep checking the oil level, and i would'nt drive it too much with that much oil leaking out. also, when you post you question, tell them if it's a 4 banger or a v6.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ronen:<BR><B>I work for a tow company as the accountant. We found an abandoned 85 Fiero GT on the side of the road and as soon as it was up for sale I bought it. I am super happy to join this family of Fiero owners. What was wrong with this abandoned was the ignition module was damaged. Once it was repaired it worked fine, but for the major oil leak. I am being told it is coming from the oil pressure sending unit. When you turn on the car the oil gage goes all the way to the above the number 80 and beyond. I looked for the oil sending unit next to the oil filter but it is not there. There is a puddle of fresh oil on the engine block right under the distributor cap area about 3 inches under the area. Is this where the sending unit actually is? How much is it to repair?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
